1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,700
Football Intelligence Platform - See the Match While You Can Still Change It

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,243
This idea started when I studied the needs of an amateur football club.

3
00:00:08,243 --> 00:00:10,201
The club could record a match,

4
00:00:10,201 --> 00:00:14,444
but information that might influence football decisions was often unavailable during the game,

5
00:00:14,444 --> 00:00:15,423
delivered too late,

6
00:00:15,423 --> 00:00:18,360
or difficult to trust without checking the video again.

7
00:00:18,360 --> 00:00:21,950
Coaches need more than footage. They need evidence they can use.

8
00:00:21,950 --> 00:00:24,608
Completed passes, possession, turnovers, shots on target,

9
00:00:24,608 --> 00:00:29,923
pitch zones and team shape matter most while the match can still be changed.

10
00:00:29,923 --> 00:00:32,580
Imagine provisional statistics updating beside the pitch,

11
00:00:32,580 --> 00:00:34,479
reaching an authorised dugout device,

12
00:00:34,479 --> 00:00:37,516
and expanding onto a dressing-room touchscreen at half-time.

13
00:00:37,516 --> 00:00:39,414
The coach remains the decision-maker,

14
00:00:39,414 --> 00:00:43,970
but can judge where possession breaks down and which areas require attention.

15
00:00:43,970 --> 00:00:47,699
The market already offers valuable camera and analytics products.

16
00:00:47,699 --> 00:00:53,086
Public entry software ranges from tens to low hundreds of euros per month,

17
00:00:53,086 --> 00:00:57,230
while hardware, live features, storage and analytics may be separate.

18
00:00:57,230 --> 00:00:59,302
Professional solutions are normally bespoke.

19
00:00:59,302 --> 00:01:03,861
The opportunity is not simply another camera. It is a shorter,

20
00:01:03,861 --> 00:01:07,590
controlled path from the action to trusted football evidence.

21
00:01:07,590 --> 00:01:12,083
Here is the proposed architecture. One elevated panoramic main camera,

22
00:01:12,083 --> 00:01:15,228
positioned on the long side near halfway,

23
00:01:15,228 --> 00:01:19,721
continuously preserves the full-pitch geometry, team spacing and off-ball movement.

24
00:01:19,721 --> 00:01:26,012
The blue and red player shapes show how the calibrated view supports tactical context.

25
00:01:26,012 --> 00:01:28,707
Green arrows connect completed passing lanes.

26
00:01:28,707 --> 00:01:32,751
The dashed amber lane shows where possession is lost.

27
00:01:32,751 --> 00:01:35,896
A second opposing panoramic camera is recommended,

28
00:01:35,896 --> 00:01:39,940
while two goal-end cameras remain optional when budget permits.

29
00:01:39,940 --> 00:01:42,835
The purple lines are infrastructure, not passes.

30
00:01:42,835 --> 00:01:54,415
Wired Cat six and Power over Ethernet feeds run around the pitch perimeter into a network switch and a locked high-speed GPU workstation in the clubhouse security office.

31
00:01:54,415 --> 00:01:56,896
Video and analysis remain locally controlled,

32
00:01:56,896 --> 00:02:01,446
with BitLocker-encrypted storage and authorised access. Overlapping thirty-second windows carry possession,

33
00:02:01,446 --> 00:02:05,581
match state, unresolved events and cumulative totals forward, suppress duplicates,

34
00:02:05,581 --> 00:02:08,890
and add each new result to the screen.

35
00:02:08,890 --> 00:02:12,056
The same provisional data can serve different decisions.

36
00:02:12,056 --> 00:02:15,221
A stadium display shows the headline match statistics.

37
00:02:15,221 --> 00:02:19,574
A future dugout view provides a concise authorised summary. At half-time,

38
00:02:19,574 --> 00:02:23,531
the larger screen reveals possession won and lost by zone,

39
00:02:23,531 --> 00:02:27,488
completed passes, final-third entries and recent trends. In this illustration,

40
00:02:27,488 --> 00:02:31,840
Zone Three is losing possession more often than it wins it,

41
00:02:31,840 --> 00:02:37,380
giving the coaching team evidence to compare with the defensive lines and match plan.

42
00:02:37,380 --> 00:02:40,971
Detection and tracking alone do not understand football.

43
00:02:40,971 --> 00:02:45,908
A law-grounded match-state engine determines whether play is live, stopped, out,

44
00:02:45,908 --> 00:02:50,846
or awaiting a restart. Event state machines evaluate control, release, reception,

45
00:02:50,846 --> 00:02:54,437
possession changes and shot outcomes. For disputed moments,

46
00:02:54,437 --> 00:02:59,823
Copilot independently reviews a focused video window before comparison with the engine.

47
00:02:59,823 --> 00:03:03,414
Authorised corrections must improve a reusable football rule,

48
00:03:03,414 --> 00:03:06,107
never one timestamp or manual label,

49
00:03:06,107 --> 00:03:08,800
and protected regressions guard accepted behaviour.

50
00:03:08,800 --> 00:03:10,758
For an amateur-club pilot,

51
00:03:10,758 --> 00:03:19,078
one panoramic main camera and secure local GPU provide the minimum viable core without mandatory cloud processing.

52
00:03:19,078 --> 00:03:23,483
Two opposing panoramic cameras are recommended for stronger coverage.

53
00:03:23,483 --> 00:03:25,930
Goal-end cameras are optional upgrades.

54
00:03:25,930 --> 00:03:31,804
An illustrative planning range is fifteen to thirty thousand euros for hardware,

55
00:03:31,804 --> 00:03:36,698
networking, secure storage, installation, calibration, initial licensing and pilot support.

56
00:03:36,698 --> 00:03:40,124
It is not a quotation; tax, connectivity,

57
00:03:40,124 --> 00:03:43,550
ongoing support and final requirements remain separate.

58
00:03:43,550 --> 00:03:48,380
Today, the working proof is offline: calibrated footage, tracking, football state,

59
00:03:48,380 --> 00:03:52,770
event review and regression-protected output. Live ingest, professional multi-camera operation,

60
00:03:52,770 --> 00:03:56,722
stadium deployment and durable player identity are next-stage capabilities,

61
00:03:56,722 --> 00:03:58,039
not completed claims.

62
00:03:58,039 --> 00:04:08,138
Our future Query By Probability concept keeps the main camera continuous and queries only the relevant secondary view for a short low-confidence moment.

63
00:04:08,138 --> 00:04:13,846
The controlled pilot target is at least ninety-five percent against independently reviewed references,

64
00:04:13,846 --> 00:04:16,480
reported separately for each agreed statistic.

65
00:04:16,480 --> 00:04:20,476
We propose a staged co-development pilot with AZ Alkmaar and Xebia:

66
00:04:20,476 --> 00:04:24,109
define the statistics that matter, agree accuracy and latency targets,

67
00:04:24,109 --> 00:04:25,562
validate on controlled matches,

68
00:04:25,562 --> 00:04:29,558
and build a credible route from grassroots affordability to professional performance.

69
00:04:29,558 --> 00:04:33,554
The goal is not more data after the moment has passed.

70
00:04:33,554 --> 00:04:38,640
It is trusted football intelligence while the next decision can still change the match.

71
00:04:38,940 --> 00:04:44,340
AZ Alkmaar and Xebia - a staged co-development pilot

